# {{ project_name }} spec

The spec is the source of truth about the system's behavior. A directory, not a single file: nobody reads the whole spec, the needed section is found by file name.

## How it works

- One file per section, named `NN-slug.md`: a two-digit section number and a short Latin name (`01-purpose.md`). The number sets the reading order and the section reference — "§N".
- Sections contain folded requirements. A version label "(1.N)" in a section's text marks which revision brought or changed the requirement.
- Spec changes go through revisions: the journal is `{{ revisions_path }}`, one file per revision (the format is in the journal README). A revision is first written to the journal, then folded into the sections, and its frontmatter gets `folded: true`.

